        <mxCell id="flow-legend" value="Flow&#10;1. Student request enters via the CloudFront WAF (Syndicate UI / LMS launch)&#10;2. Edge (CloudFront) serves the UI and forwards API calls to SEP (se-ui-api REST)&#10;3. Operator drives SEP via the management API / CLI&#10;4. LMS launches SEP via LTI 1.0/1.1&#10;5. Keycloak validates the corporate SSO token for SEP&#10;6. SEP reads/writes application data in MongoDB Atlas (over VPC peering)&#10;7. SEP ⇄ Syndicate Server over SQS: sandbox/org lifecycle (the in-account control plane)&#10;8. License Manager -&gt; SEP (sep-lm-synchronization-queue -&gt; se-management-api-handler)&#10;9. SEP calls AI providers (Bedrock / DIAL) for Syndi / Angry EdA&#10;10. SEP returns task results to the LMS over LTI grade passback (AGS)&#10;11. WAF (syndicate_education_cloudfront_waf, global) relays to CloudFront&#10;12. Syndicate Server provisions and cleans up the multi-cloud sandbox fleets" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=#B3B3B3;fillColor=#FFFFFF;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1138" y="60" width="300" height="404" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" value="Legend&#10;Solid line = primary flow&#10;Dashed line = asynchronous / event-driven flow&#10;Red = blocked / missing / disabled&#10;🆕 = new in version N&#10;🔄 = changed in version N&#10;Outer boundary = stack Boundary (captioned; provider style)&#10;Numbered markers (1..N) = ordered data flow steps; see Flow list&#10;callout 'draft-assumption' = unconfirmed path, first-draft assumption&#10;WAF = syndicate_education_cloudfront_waf (global, fronts CloudFront)&#10;Sandbox fleets = multi-cloud sandbox accounts (AWS/Azure/GCP), provisioned + cleaned by the Syndicate Server" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=#B3B3B3;fillColor=#FFFFFF;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1138" y="474" width="300" height="292" as="geometry" />
